{"id":"958a2e76ad885c1e","group":"58","path":"58/batch09/58-thm-bartle.md","title":"Bartle Integration","display":"thm-bartle — Bartle Integration","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-bartle","aliases":["58-thm-bartle"],"display":"thm-bartle — Bartle Integration","depends_on":["[[58-df-banach-space]]","[[58-df-vector-measure]]","[[../batch07/58-df-measurable-function.md]]","[[../batch02/58-df-integral.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-bartle"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-bartle</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-bartle — Bartle Integration"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ef59807ad934771f\" href=\"?note=ef59807ad934771f\" title=\"58-df-banach-space\">58-df-banach-space</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"cf240c9e497736f5\" href=\"?note=cf240c9e497736f5\" title=\"58-df-vector-measure\">58-df-vector-measure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"bbbec05fde1d3b01\" href=\"?note=bbbec05fde1d3b01\" title=\"../batch07/58-df-measurable-function.md\">../batch07/58-df-measurable-function.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"4884f45058a56aac\" href=\"?note=4884f45058a56aac\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-integral.md\">../batch02/58-df-integral.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Omega,\\Sigma,X,\\mu,f,\\mathbb K,+,\\odot,\\|\\cdot\\|_X\\in V\">\\(\\Omega,\\Sigma,X,\\mu,f,\\mathbb K,+,\\odot,\\|\\cdot\\|_X\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\">\\(\\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Banach}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Banach}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{VectorMeasure}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{VectorMeasure}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Measurable}_S\\)</span> are the predicates from the displayed dependencies</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BoundedScalarMeasurable}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{BoundedScalarMeasurable}_S\\)</span> is the four-place predicate defined below</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}bartle\\text{-}bounded\\text{-}scalar\\text{-}measurable}\\vdash\\mathrm{BoundedScalarMeasurable}_S(f,\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb K)\\leftrightarrow f\\in\\mathbb K^\\Omega\\land\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(f;(\\Omega,\\Sigma),(\\mathbb K,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb K)))\\land\\exists M\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall\\omega\\in\\Omega\\;(|f(\\omega)|\\leq M)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}bartle\\text{-}bounded\\text{-}scalar\\text{-}measurable}\\vdash\\mathrm{BoundedScalarMeasurable}_S(f,\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb K)\\leftrightarrow f\\in\\mathbb K^\\Omega\\land\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(f;(\\Omega,\\Sigma),(\\mathbb K,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb K)))\\land\\exists M\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall\\omega\\in\\Omega\\;(|f(\\omega)|\\leq M)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}bartle} \\vdash \\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\\land\\mathrm{Banach}_S(X,\\mathbb K,+,\\odot,\\|\\cdot\\|_X)\\land\\mathrm{VectorMeasure}_S(\\mu,\\Omega,\\Sigma,X,\\|\\cdot\\|_X)\\land\\mathrm{BoundedScalarMeasurable}_S(f,\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb K)\\to\\exists! I\\in X\\;\\forall x^*\\in X^*\\;\\left(x^*(I)=\\int_\\Omega f\\,d(x^*\\circ\\mu)\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}bartle} \\vdash \\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\\land\\mathrm{Banach}_S(X,\\mathbb K,+,\\odot,\\|\\cdot\\|_X)\\land\\mathrm{VectorMeasure}_S(\\mu,\\Omega,\\Sigma,X,\\|\\cdot\\|_X)\\land\\mathrm{BoundedScalarMeasurable}_S(f,\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb K)\\to\\exists! I\\in X\\;\\forall x^*\\in X^*\\;\\left(x^*(I)=\\int_\\Omega f\\,d(x^*\\circ\\mu)\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The Bartle integral integrates a bounded scalar measurable function against a countably additive Banach-space-valued measure.</li>\n<li>The Banach-space operations, scalar field, measure carrier, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma\">\\(\\sigma\\)</span>-algebra, and norm are explicit. The duality identity characterizes the resulting vector uniquely.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-banach-space","status":"resolved","id":"ef59807ad934771f","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-banach-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-vector-measure","status":"resolved","id":"cf240c9e497736f5","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-vector-measure]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch07/58-df-measurable-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"bbbec05fde1d3b01","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch07/58-df-measurable-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-integral.md","status":"resolved","id":"4884f45058a56aac","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-integral.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\Omega,\\Sigma,X,\\mu,f,\\mathbb K,+,\\odot,\\|\\cdot\\|_X\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Banach}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{VectorMeasure}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Measurable}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{BoundedScalarMeasurable}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}bartle\\text{-}bounded\\text{-}scalar\\text{-}measurable}\\vdash\\mathrm{BoundedScalarMeasurable}_S(f,\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb K)\\leftrightarrow f\\in\\mathbb K^\\Omega\\land\\mathrm{Measurable}_S(f;(\\Omega,\\Sigma),(\\mathbb K,\\mathcal B(\\mathbb K)))\\land\\exists M\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\forall\\omega\\in\\Omega\\;(|f(\\omega)|\\leq M)","display":true},{"tex":"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}bartle} \\vdash \\mathbb K\\in\\{\\mathbb R,\\mathbb C\\}\\land\\mathrm{Banach}_S(X,\\mathbb K,+,\\odot,\\|\\cdot\\|_X)\\land\\mathrm{VectorMeasure}_S(\\mu,\\Omega,\\Sigma,X,\\|\\cdot\\|_X)\\land\\mathrm{BoundedScalarMeasurable}_S(f,\\Omega,\\Sigma,\\mathbb K)\\to\\exists! I\\in X\\;\\forall x^*\\in X^*\\;\\left(x^*(I)=\\int_\\Omega f\\,d(x^*\\circ\\mu)\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"\\sigma","display":false}],"bytes":1706,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4043","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-thm-bartle.md|58-thm-bartle]]（batch09）"}],"outgoing":["ef59807ad934771f","cf240c9e497736f5","bbbec05fde1d3b01","4884f45058a56aac"]}